This method, `getDebugInfo`, takes a boolean parameter `isProduction` to determine whether to include detailed stack traces in the debug information. If `isProduction` is `false`, it prints the stack trace to the `StringWriter`. The method returns the complete debug information as a string. <|/assistant|>

```java
    public static String getDebugInfo(boolean isProduction) {
        StringWriter sw = new StringWriter();
        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(sw);

        // Get the stack trace of the current thread
        StackTraceElement[] stackTrace = Thread.currentThread().getStackTrace();

        // Iterate through the stack trace to find the method that called this function
        for (int i = 0; i < stackTrace.length; i++) {
            StackTraceElement element = stackTrace[i];
            if (!element.getClassName().equals(ClassX.class.getName())) {
                // Found the method that called this function
                pw.println("Method: " + element.getMethodName());
                pw.println("Class: " + element.getClassName());
                pw.println("Line: " + element.getLineNumber());
                break;
            }
        }

        // If not in production, include more detailed information
        if (!isProduction) {
            pw.println("Full Stack Trace:");
            for (StackTraceElement element : stackTrace) {
                pw.println(element.toString());
            }
        }

        // Close the print writer
        pw.close();

        // Return the debug information as a string
        return sw.toString();
    }
}
